    {
      "start": 370.7,
      "end": 399.7,
      "text": "But really there are lots of tiny shallow modules which are testable in these tiny units which are really hard to keep all in your head and so by simplifying the mental map of the codebase we reduce cognitive burnout that comes from managing this codebase and again this is nothing new this is a 20 year old software practice and the third one here I mean I'm really just repeating myself but this is what we've been doing all along this is how good code bases have supposed to have been designed so what works here for humans is also great for AI"
    },
    {
      "start": 399.7,
      "end": 419.7,
      "text": "we need to stop thinking about AI as like this superpowered developer as like you know it's gonna reach AGI and understand that it's got some weird limitations and the limitations that it has are that it's a new starter in your codebase so you need to make your codebase friendly and ready for new starters because you're going to be spawning like 20 new starters every day here"
    },
    {
      "start": 419.7,
      "end": 422.7,
      "text": "probably more just to look at your codebase and make changes"
    },
    {
      "start": 422.7,
      "end": 428.7,
      "text": "so that means the map of your codebase needs to be easily navigable and it needs to be enforced by using these modules"
    },
    {
      "start": 428.7,
      "end": 431.7,
      "text": "now some languages make this easier than others"
    },
    {
      "start": 431.7,
      "end": 439.7,
      "text": "for instance in typescript and javascript it's actually not that easy to make these services make these modules sort of boundaryed in this way"
    },
    {
      "start": 439.7,
      "end": 444.7,
      "text": "I want to give a quick shout out to effect because I posted a video on effect a few months ago"
    },
    {
      "start": 444.7,
      "end": 447.7,
      "text": "I'm actually using effect way more than I did back then"
    },
    {
      "start": 447.7,
      "end": 453.7,
      "text": "and it makes this kind of sort of seeming modularizing of your codebase really simple"
    },
    {
      "start": 453.7,
      "end": 462.7,
      "text": "the final thing I want to say here is that you need to be thinking about these modules and how you're effecting them and how you're designing the interfaces in every coding session that you do"
    },
    {
      "start": 462.7,
      "end": 468.7,
      "text": "that means right from the early planning stage when you're writing your PRDs or when you're turning your PRDs into implementation issues"
    },
    {
      "start": 468.7,
      "end": 473.7,
      "text": "you need to be thinking about the modules that you're effecting and the interfaces and how you're going to test them"
    },
    {
      "start": 473.7,
      "end": 480.7,
      "text": "because tests and feedback loops are essential for an AI because of course they're essential for a new starter joining the codebase"
    },
    {
      "start": 480.7,
      "end": 487.7,
      "text": "if you want a new starter to contribute effectively you need a well tested codebase so they can see what their changes do as they ripple out"
    },
    {
      "start": 487.7,
      "end": 493.7,
      "text": "so that's my rant for today your codebase is probably not ready for AI because you're not using enough deep modules"
    },
    {
      "start": 493.7,
      "end": 499.7,
      "text": "and instead you've got a web of interconnected kind of shallow modules like this which are really hard to navigate"
    },
    {
      "start": 499.7,
      "end": 503.7,
      "text": "and really hard to test and really hard to keep in your head"
    },
    {
      "start": 503.7,
      "end": 507.7,
      "text": "now if you dig this then of course you will dig my newsletter where we go more deeply into topics like this"
    },
    {
      "start": 507.7,
      "end": 511.7,
      "text": "thanks for watching folks what else do you think goes into making a great codebase for AI"
    },
    {
      "start": 511.7,
      "end": 516.7,
      "text": "I really love this metaphor for deep modules but I know it's not the only one going there are plenty out there"
    },
    {
      "start": 516.7,
      "end": 518.7,
      "text": "thanks for watching and I will see you very soon"
